  "question": {
    "text": "Two magnets of equal mass are joined at 90<math><mo>°</mo></math> each other as shown in figure. Magnet <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> has a magnetic moment <math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> times that of <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>. The arrangement is pivoted so that it is free to rotate in horizontal plane. When in equilibrium, what angle should <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> make with magnetic meridian?<br />\r<br />\r&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Phys_28.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 120px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
