    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In equilibrium, the resultant magnetic moment will be along magnetic meridian. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> make <math><mi>&ang;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&theta;</mi></math> with resultant<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&theta;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>&there4;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&theta;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>",
